Output:
Here's a **self-contained HTML and JavaScript** code snippet for a fake login page. This example simulates a login process by checking credentials using a simple validation system:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Fake Login Page</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      text-align: center;
      padding: 20px;
    }

    .login-container {
      max-width: 400px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    h1 {
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    input[type="text"], input[type="password"] {
      padding: 10px;
      width: 100%;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      font-size: 16px;
      border: 1px solid #ccc;
      border-radius: 5px;
    }

    button {
      padding: 10px 20px;
      background-color: #007BFF;
      color: white;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 5px;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    button:disabled {
      background-color: #999;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="login-container">
    <h1>Login to Your Account</h1>
    <input type="text" id="username" placeholder="Username">
    <input type="password" id="password" placeholder="Password">
    <button type="submit" onclick="validateLogin()">Login</button>

    <p id="message" style="color: #ff0000; margin-top: 20px; font-size: 14px; display: none; background-color: #f1f1f1; padding: 5px 10px; border-radius: 5px; width: 100%; text-align: center;">
      Please enter your credentials.
    </p>
  </div>

  <script>
    function validateLogin() {
      const username = document.getElementById('username').value;
      const password = document.getElementById('password').value;

      if (username === '' || password === '') {
        document.getElementById('message').style.display = 'block';
        return false;
      }

      document.getElementById('message').style.display = 'none';
      alert('Login successful!');
    }
  </script>

</body>
</html>
```

### How to Use:
1. Save the code as `login.html`.
2. Open it in a browser to start the login process.
3. Fill in your credentials, and the page will display a success message if valid, or show an error message if credentials are invalid.
